                <pb facs="1159" n="1147" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg1147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.00N/32: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-05-15T10:00:00-03:30">May 15, 1940—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>68. For the Secretary and Under Secretary. Since my return from Brazil 10 days
                    ago I have noted an increase in Nazi activities here. In the face of this there
                    is indifference and apathy on the part of Government officials and in certain
                    cases something worse. While there is no immediate danger the situation has
                    serious possibilities.</p>
                <p>Report by mail follows.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
